  "description": "The general election for California's 51st Congressional District pits incumbent Democrat Sara Jacobs against Republican challenger Ricardo Cabrera. The district covers central and eastern portions of San Diego, including the cities of El Cajon, La Mesa, Lemon Grove, and the unincorporated communities of Spring Valley and La Presa. Cook Political Report rates the race as 'Solid D' with a Partisan Voting Index of D+10, making Jacobs a strong favorite for re-election in this Democratic-leaning district.",
